It was definitely due to the huge number of monsters that you
genocided.  Actually whenever you genocide a monster you increase the
chance of an Angel or other high level casters, being generated in a
monster summon. So the more monsters you have genocided the higher the
chance.

Once you have the Amulet the Difficulty of Monsters generated is the
average of Sanctum level, and your level, ie ~27+XL/2. While in the
Planes it is Average of Sanctum level + XL/2 and XL, ie ~27+XL. So for
your run the DIF or monsters is ~38 and in the end game ~50. In
addition no monsters will be generated that have a difficulty level
less than your dungeon level/7, ie 8 during run and 10 in the endgame.

If you look up the monster spoilers you will see that very few
monsters qualify for generation that have not been genocided.
1) Winged Gargoyle
2) giant mimic
3) titanothere
4) mastodon
5) baluchitherium
6) lurker above
7) trapper
8) All Angels
9) Vampire and Vampire lord
10) Xorn
11) Nazgul
12) Golems
13) Titan

You see that there are very few monsters left that apart from the
spellcasters.  So beware of genociding too many classes of
monsters. At the very least never genocide H,T, and D. Because these
help to reduce the summoning storms a lot.

I would think that L, ; and *mindflayers, Disenchanter, green slime
are the only good monsters to be genocided. Actually you don't need to
use more than two blessed scrolls of genocide, and 4 uncursed genocide
scrolls.

Even better use is to curse them for nurse dancing and summoning
intrinsic granting Dragons. If you play carefully and have MR you can
live without any genocidings.

